From: The412Banner <205237651+The412Banner@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zink: skip dma-buf implicit sync when no exportable semaphore
 can be created

zink_screen_export_dmabuf_semaphore() exports the dma-buf's sync file and
imports it into a semaphore from zink_create_exportable_semaphore(). That
returns VK_NULL_HANDLE when the driver's vkCreateSemaphore() fails for a
SYNC_FD-exportable semaphore, and the null handle went straight into
vkImportSemaphoreFdKHR() with VK_SEMAPHORE_IMPORT_TEMPORARY_BIT. The
common runtime then reads the semaphore's type through a null pointer.

On PanVK for Arm's kbase driver (Mali-G57 MC2, MT6789) Xwayland's glamor
crashed this way, at address 0x40 in vk_common_ImportSemaphoreFdKHR(), the
first time it used a client's dma-buf, and gamescope aborted with it. Treat
the failure like a failed sync file export: close the sync file and return
VK_NULL_HANDLE, which the caller already skips. Still present in Mesa main.
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -2458,6 +2458,15 @@
    }
 
    sem = zink_create_exportable_semaphore(screen);
+   if (unlikely(!sem)) {
+      static bool warned;
+      if (!warned) {
+         warned = true;
+         mesa_loge("MESA: Unable to create an exportable semaphore; skipping implicit sync for dma-bufs");
+      }
+      close(export.fd);
+      return VK_NULL_HANDLE;
+   }
 
    const VkImportSemaphoreFdInfoKHR sdi = {
       .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_IMPORT_SEMAPHORE_FD_INFO_KHR,
